  "termsTitle": "Terms and privacy",
  "termsLead": "This app talks to a mesh radio. There is no account, no cloud and no analytics.",
  "termsSectionLocal": "WHAT STAYS ON THIS DEVICE",
  "termsLocalBody": "Messages, contacts, channels and settings are stored on this device. Message history, places, the movement trail and geofences are encrypted with a key this phone holds and cannot export. Coverage cells are session-only, so nothing about them is written at all. Cloud backup and device transfer are off for everything, so a new phone does not silently inherit it. Deleting the app deletes that data.",
  "termsSectionLeaves": "WHAT LEAVES THE DEVICE",
  "termsLeavesBody": "Two things leave this device. What you send goes out over the radio you are connected to: messages, positions and reactions. And the map asks a tile server for map squares, which tells that server roughly where you are looking; the map names the source it is using. Offline map packs are off by default and are fetched only after you turn them on. Nothing else leaves. Files you export are yours to place.",
  "termsSectionPermissions": "PERMISSIONS AND WHY",
  "termsPermissionsBody": "Bluetooth connects to the radio. Location is used for your own position and, on older Android, to allow a Bluetooth scan. Notifications are used for messages that arrive while the app is in the background. Refusing any of them leaves the app usable without a radio.",
  "termsSectionRetention": "HOW MUCH IS KEPT",
  "termsRetentionBody": "Each conversation keeps its newest {cap} messages; older ones are dropped. A place expires when its own timer runs out, and is then gone.",
  "@termsRetentionBody": {
    "placeholders": {
      "cap": {
        "type": "int"
      }
    }
